WEBVTT

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.130
Zero kara kakedashite

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.130
Start running from the beginning,

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:08.500
Omoi dake wo dakishimete

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:08.500
with nothing but your emotions in your hands.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.890
Sonomama kakenukete

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.890
Just keep running...

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:18.350
Itsumo koko de mitsumeteru

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:18.350
I'm always watching you from here.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:42.300
Hajimete deatta hi no manazashi wasurenai

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:42.300
I still remember your expression the day we first met.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:49.190
Taiyou mitai ni kokoro wo terashitekureta

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:49.190
It lit up my heart like the sun.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:56.960
Asu no yukue sagashite nayandeiru nara

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:56.960
If you're anxious about where to go tomorrow,

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:06.890
Ima kimi no tame ni akari ni naritai yo

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:06.890
I want to become a beacon to you.

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.010
Zero kara tobidatte

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.010
Start flying from the beginning.

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:16.380
Ima no kimi wo toki hanachi

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:16.380
Let go of your current self...

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:19.730
Mugen ni habataite

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:19.730
and fly towards infinity.

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:23.600
Donna toki mo mimaru yo

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:23.600
I will always watch over you...

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:29.510
Kitto zutto tooku made

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:29.510
no matter how far you fly.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:36.080
Episode 33 - The Miracle of the Outdoor Theater

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:39.780
So, what are you guys going to do about admissions?

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:46.100
Well, this show is really just an experiment for us to test our skills.

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:48.700
All we ask is that people sit and watch.

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:50.050
Otherwise...

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:53.610
how else can we expect anyone to watch a show put on by an anonymous troupe like us?

00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:57.940
Is that how much you think your talents are worth?

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:00.670
Listen up.

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:02.670
You gain nothing by cheapening your performance.

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:04.850
Have some pride and charge an admission fee.

00:02:05.210 --> 00:02:07.750
Give all proceeds to a welfare organization.

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:10.980
Then, you can advertise the show as a charity event.

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:15.260
Just let everyone in the audience donate what they feel is appropriate and then, collect it up.

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:19.700
If they like the play, I'm sure the audience will be more than willing to donate money to a good cause.

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:22.550
It goes without saying that you won't see any of the money because it's a charity event,

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:26.850
but I'm sure you'll gain something even more valuable from the experience.

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:32.360
Thank you very much for the advice, Mr. Hayami!

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:38.480
What's with that look?

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:41.110
You're being awfully nice,

00:02:41.110 --> 00:02:44.660
for someone who's reputedly a lifer in Daito Entertainment.

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:48.680
You like to speak your mind, don't you?

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:49.970
Oh, does that bother you?

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:53.270
No, you don't bother me at all.

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:59.470
After all, I'm surrounded by sycophants every day.

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:05.480
Ms. Tsukikage won't be able to come to your show.

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:10.720
Relax. She just needs some rest and she'll be fine.

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:13.720
Don't struggle, okay?

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:15.950
Excuse me...

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:17.270
Sit here.

00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:20.640
Quickly!

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:26.500
I want to know how you really feel.

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:29.430
About <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:34.480
Now that she's won Japan's most prestigious acting award, you pretty much have no chance...

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:38.210
of competing with Ayumi Himekawa.

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:39.420
I know.

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:44.270
If you think you don't have a chance, I'd like you to forfeit.

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:47.430
There must be more to life than <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>.

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:51.370
If you give me your word that you'll give up on <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>,

00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:55.460
I'll reestablish you in the acting world.

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:57.500
Mr. Hayami...

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:04.960
I wouldn't give up on <i>The Scarlet Angel</i> even if the whole world told me...

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:09.600
there was no way I could get it.

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:13.570
Ayumi told me she would wait two years for me!

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:22.600
When everyone else was telling me that I couldn't do it, she told me she'd wait for me.

00:04:23.380 --> 00:04:27.570
If I forfeit now, Ayumi will lose all respect for me.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:32.510
And she's the only person in the world whose respect matters to me!

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:37.450
Honestly, I don't believe I can win such a prestigious award in the next two years,

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:40.080
but I don't want to throw away the possibility!

00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:48.310
I see. Then, Daito will withdraw completely from this matter.

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:55.190
You know, Mr. Hayami... I have a dream.

00:04:55.190 --> 00:05:00.420
I have a dream of inviting a certain person to my next major production if I'm ever in one.

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:05.350
I don't even know his name, but he's a very dear fan of mine.

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:09.920
He's never shown himself to me before, but just once, I'd love to meet him.

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:16.680
And what if you meet him and find out it's someone you don't like one little bit?

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:18.430
How could that even be possible?

00:05:18.430 --> 00:05:22.170
I'm sure I'd like him, no matter what kind of person he turns out to be.

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:27.300
Even if the whole world hates him!

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:32.450
And what if that person... what if he turned out to be...

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:41.220
It's so bright today...

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:44.930
I'd forgotten how bright the sun was.

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:53.940
We're performing a charity play in the local open-air theater!

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:57.250
Please come see it!

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:59.930
No-one's even looking at us!

00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:07.830
Looks like you guys are having a tough time out here.

00:06:07.830 --> 00:06:10.000
Even your street-performer publicity looks bland.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:11.150
You trying to start something?!

00:06:10.540 --> 00:06:15.700
<i>A Midsummer Night's Dream</i>

00:06:12.950 --> 00:06:15.730
You called us street performers.

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:23.740
Well, street performers have tricks of their own.

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:28.260
Come one! Come all!

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:32.540
Puck is my name and I'm a woodland sprite!

00:06:32.930 --> 00:06:38.410
What will happen when these two lovers meet in the middle of the forest?

00:06:38.770 --> 00:06:41.560
<i>A Midsummer Night's Dream!</i>

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:43.950
The flash of summer's heat...

00:06:43.950 --> 00:06:45.770
A dream in midsummer...

00:06:45.770 --> 00:06:49.880
We wish to bestow our wonderful dream upon all who gather here!

00:06:52.710 --> 00:06:53.780
Maya?

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:58.260
I don't know what's got into me. I haven't felt this good for ages!

00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:01.600
Two hours left till showtime!

00:07:01.930 --> 00:07:06.070
The next three days will test us to the max!

00:07:06.070 --> 00:07:09.680
Let's make our show so good that everyone that comes today will come...

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:11.300
and see it again tomorrow!

00:07:18.260 --> 00:07:20.960
Maya, what are you doing?

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:24.770
I was just listening to the wind. Listen!

00:07:24.770 --> 00:07:28.050
When it blows, you can hear the leaves rustling.

00:07:28.790 --> 00:07:33.070
I feel so lucky, playing a fairy on an outdoor stage!

00:07:33.330 --> 00:07:35.520
She was listening to the wind...

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:39.070
This is one hell of a set we've got here!

00:07:40.050 --> 00:07:43.540
She's using the set pieces and the backdrop to its fullest.

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:45.800
Impressive.

00:07:46.060 --> 00:07:46.910
Maya.

00:07:48.110 --> 00:07:49.410
Mr. Hijiri!

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:52.560
He's sent you these to congratulate you on your show today.

00:07:53.650 --> 00:07:56.520
He will be in the audience today.

00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:57.970
Really?

00:08:08.600 --> 00:08:12.710
We still have an hour until the curtain goes up and yet...

00:08:13.310 --> 00:08:14.720
Can you please pack in more?

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:18.330
It's the Tsukikage Acting Troupe and the Ikkakujuu Troupe from that basement theater.

00:08:19.110 --> 00:08:20.380
But that's impossible!

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:22.820
There's still an hour to go till the show starts!

00:08:22.820 --> 00:08:25.050
And they've still got more and more people coming in.

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:28.830
A lot of their regular fans from their basement theater are here too.

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:30.050
At this rate...

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:59.460
The Tsukikage Acting Troupe and the Ikkakujuu Troupe would like to thank you all for coming...

00:08:59.460 --> 00:09:02.510
to our outdoor premier tonight!

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:05.380
Look over there.

00:09:05.380 --> 00:09:08.070
It's Masumi Hayami and Hyuuga, the famous playwright.

00:09:08.530 --> 00:09:16.660
And now, for tonight's dream: Everyone, open your eyes wide!

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:18.010
A purple rose!

00:09:19.990 --> 00:09:23.050
Did you see that, Mr. Purple Roses?

00:09:23.050 --> 00:09:25.810
That was a message to you!

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:32.200
<i>A Midsummer Night's Dream</i>, Act One, Scene One.

00:09:32.430 --> 00:09:36.450
The fair Hermia is on the verge of being forcefully engaged to a suitor proposed by her father...

00:09:36.450 --> 00:09:39.680
A man by the name of Demetrius.

00:09:40.690 --> 00:09:42.860
What say you, Hermia?

00:09:42.860 --> 00:09:45.500
Demetrius is a worthy gentleman.

00:09:45.500 --> 00:09:49.570
Yet, Hermia loves another; a young man by the name Lysander.

00:09:49.570 --> 00:09:52.750
So is Lysander.

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:54.340
Relent, sweet Hermia.

00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:59.070
You have her father's love, Demetrius;

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:01.600
let me have Hermia's:

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:04.180
do you marry him.

00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:09.790
This is fantastic. The audience's really getting into it!

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:11.390
We can do this!

00:10:11.830 --> 00:10:14.320
The two vow to run away together.

00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:17.380
They makes plans to meet each other in a forest on the edge of Athens.

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:20.150
I will, my Hermia.

00:10:22.450 --> 00:10:24.410
It's Keiko!

00:10:25.460 --> 00:10:28.700
God speed fair Helena!

00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:30.270
Whither away?

00:10:32.890 --> 00:10:36.500
Call you me fair? That fair again unsay.

00:10:36.770 --> 00:10:40.430
Demetrius loves your fair:

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:43.880
O happy fair!

00:10:44.280 --> 00:10:48.550
Helena has lost her heart to Demetrius, but she is also Hermia's friend.

00:10:48.970 --> 00:10:54.840
Take comfort, Helena: he no more shall see my face;

00:10:55.230 --> 00:11:01.690
Lysander and myself will fly this place.

00:11:02.150 --> 00:11:05.860
Farewell, sweet playfellow: pray thou for us;

00:11:05.860 --> 00:11:11.210
And good luck grant thee thy Demetrius!

00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:18.220
But, even though she loves him, Helena tells Demetrius of their plans.

00:11:18.970 --> 00:11:25.290
Demetrius ventures deep into the forest to reclaim Hermia and Helena follows him.

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:50.310
And now we come to the best part of the play: Act Two!

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:51.930
We're counting on you, Maya!

00:11:51.930 --> 00:11:52.780
I know.

00:12:04.220 --> 00:12:07.050
I am that merry wanderer of the night.

00:12:07.050 --> 00:12:08.480
For I am Puck!

00:12:08.480 --> 00:12:11.050
I serve the fairy king, Oberon!

00:12:11.380 --> 00:12:14.830
Of late, Oberon is passing fell and wrath,

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:17.690
take heed the queen come not within his sight!

00:12:19.430 --> 00:12:22.440
Ill met by moonlight,

00:12:22.440 --> 00:12:24.970
proud Titania!

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:28.480
What, jealous Oberon!

00:12:28.800 --> 00:12:31.220
Tarry, rash wanton,

00:12:31.220 --> 00:12:33.480
am not I thy lord?

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:37.310
When thou hast stolen away from fairy land, and in the shape of Corin...

00:12:37.310 --> 00:12:40.900
sat all day, playing on pipes of corn...

00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:45.730
and versing love to amorous Phillida.

00:12:45.730 --> 00:12:49.050
Why not become human and end such farce?

00:12:49.270 --> 00:12:55.840
Why should Titania cross her Oberon? I do but beg a little changeling boy, to be my henchman.

00:12:55.840 --> 00:12:58.840
Set your heart at rest.

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:01.250
This insolence!

00:13:02.930 --> 00:13:04.160
My lord, Oberon!

00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:07.560
Fetch me that little western flower; the herb I shew'd thee once.

00:13:07.560 --> 00:13:08.900
The western flower...

00:13:08.900 --> 00:13:11.980
The juice of it on sleeping eye-lids laid...

00:13:11.980 --> 00:13:15.890
will make man or woman madly dote upon the next live creature that it sees.

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:17.450
That very one.

00:13:17.450 --> 00:13:22.480
I'll put a girdle round about the earth in forty minutes.

00:13:24.590 --> 00:13:27.690
Spin earth, spin!

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:35.330
Her instincts tell her how she should be moving on stage.

00:13:36.200 --> 00:13:39.610
She's able to create the illusion of wind.

00:13:40.520 --> 00:13:44.470
How on earth am I meant to have any presence on stage after that?

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:53.960
On this longest of summer nights, upon thy I throw all the power this charm doth owe.

00:13:53.960 --> 00:13:56.690
When thou wakest, let love forbid sleep his seat on thy eyelid.

00:13:56.690 --> 00:14:00.190
The man shall have his mare!

00:14:02.680 --> 00:14:05.740
Lysander! On the ground! Dead? Or asleep?

00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:08.190
If you live, good sir, awake.

00:14:11.100 --> 00:14:14.210
What ails you, Lysander?

00:14:14.650 --> 00:14:16.580
Transparent Helena!

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:20.370
Nature shows art, that through thy bosom makes me see thy heart.

00:14:20.370 --> 00:14:24.360
And run through fire I will for thy sweet sake.

00:14:25.030 --> 00:14:27.850
Wherefore was I to this keen mockery born?

00:14:27.850 --> 00:14:28.820
What though he love your Hermia?

00:14:28.820 --> 00:14:30.480
I know her not.

00:14:31.880 --> 00:14:34.470
And yet you fly with her!

00:14:37.240 --> 00:14:39.970
Oh Bottom, thou art changed! An ass's nole upon your noggin!

00:14:39.970 --> 00:14:43.650
The queen waked and straightway loved an ass.

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:44.970
This falls out better than I could devise, Puck.

00:14:45.240 --> 00:14:48.510
What's this to my Lysander? Where is he?

00:14:48.510 --> 00:14:49.980
You spend your passion on a misprised mood, Hermia.

00:14:49.980 --> 00:14:51.630
O, why rebuke you him that loves you so?

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:53.280
What hast thou done?

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:56.210
Thou hast mistaken quite and laid the love-juice on some true-love's sight.

00:14:56.480 --> 00:15:03.200
About the wood go swifter than the wind, and Helena of Athens look thou find.

00:15:03.200 --> 00:15:04.460
I go, I go; look how I go,

00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:06.470
Swifter than arrow from the Tartar's bow.

00:15:06.470 --> 00:15:08.390
Go Puck!

00:15:09.700 --> 00:15:15.730
When thou wakest, if she be by, beg of her for remedy.

00:15:18.230 --> 00:15:23.800
Woken by the sound of quarreling, Demetrius first espies the once-despised Helena.

00:15:24.070 --> 00:15:27.390
O Helena, goddess, nymph, perfect, divine!

00:15:28.210 --> 00:15:29.530
O spite! O hell!

00:15:29.530 --> 00:15:32.200
It is Helena whom I do love and will do till death.

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:35.230
I see you are all bent to set against me for your merriment.

00:15:35.630 --> 00:15:38.200
My Lysander, why unkindly didst thou leave so?

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:41.690
You are unkind, Demetrius; be not so: for you love Hermia.

00:15:43.640 --> 00:15:47.130
Lysander, keep thy Hermia; I will none.

00:15:47.420 --> 00:15:53.070
If e'er I loved her, all that love is gone.

00:15:53.070 --> 00:15:54.470
Helena!

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:00.140
Hie Puck!

00:16:00.140 --> 00:16:02.470
Open up the gates of darkness!

00:16:02.470 --> 00:16:07.200
Now, return thee hence these tangl'd threads.

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:08.900
I come, my fairy lord!

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:10.210
My time cometh!

00:16:10.210 --> 00:16:13.580
Let's get warmed up first!

00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:34.230
On the ground, sleep sound.

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:41.650
Close thy lids, and when thou wakest, thou takest true delight in the sight...

00:16:41.650 --> 00:16:44.230
of thy former lady's eye.

00:16:49.600 --> 00:16:52.100
Take this hysteria as truth,

00:16:52.100 --> 00:16:54.920
for the tale depicts thy discordant dreams.

00:16:55.390 --> 00:16:57.190
I beg you; challenge them not.

00:16:57.190 --> 00:17:04.290
One last favor must I ask for this spectacle to complete;

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:06.740
a token of thy goodwill!

00:17:07.020 --> 00:17:12.780
All who gather here, clap thy hands like this: Papan ga pan!

00:17:12.780 --> 00:17:14.290
Papan ga pan!

00:17:14.290 --> 00:17:14.950
Once more!

00:17:14.950 --> 00:17:16.170
Papan ga pan!

00:17:16.170 --> 00:17:16.770
Once more!

00:17:16.770 --> 00:17:18.340
Papan ga pan!

00:17:23.700 --> 00:17:27.100
She's got the audience in the palm of her hand.

00:17:27.360 --> 00:17:30.640
We'll take any donations here.

00:17:31.180 --> 00:17:35.120
Mr. Purple Roses is here somewhere.

00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:39.160
I wish he'd come and talk to me. Even if all he says is "Good job."

00:17:39.160 --> 00:17:40.370
Good job.

00:17:40.610 --> 00:17:43.290
Your Puck was very vibrant!

00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:46.170
I'm glad you liked it.

00:17:48.740 --> 00:17:49.440
That much?!

00:17:49.740 --> 00:17:52.310
It's not like I'm giving it to <i>you</i>.

00:17:52.310 --> 00:17:53.500
It's going to charity.

00:17:54.690 --> 00:17:57.000
You've gotten quite good, little one.

00:17:57.950 --> 00:17:59.910
<i>A Midsummer Night's Dream</i> - Fundraiser Performance

00:18:01.950 --> 00:18:04.540
Kazuya Tamura

00:18:02.030 --> 00:18:04.560
Daito Entertainment wants to produce our play?

00:18:04.560 --> 00:18:07.560
You mean the show at the Athena Theater?

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:13.150
Wait a second. Why would a company as big as Daito be interested in us?

00:18:13.410 --> 00:18:17.550
Mr. Hyuuga, the famous playwright, was in the audience at your last show...

00:18:17.550 --> 00:18:20.230
and he said he really wanted to promote you guys.

00:18:21.530 --> 00:18:25.680
With our backing, I'm sure you'll become huge.

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:30.000
Daito Entertainment

00:18:27.760 --> 00:18:30.720
You're plotting something, aren't you?

00:18:30.720 --> 00:18:35.680
I won't forgive you if you try anything to sabotage our group!

00:18:38.280 --> 00:18:40.100
What's so funny?!

00:18:40.670 --> 00:18:44.860
You're the first person who's ever been that forthright with me.

00:18:45.400 --> 00:18:48.840
Okay, then I guess you deserve a straight answer.

00:18:48.840 --> 00:18:50.470
I have no ulterior motives.

00:18:51.120 --> 00:18:53.890
My only wish is to create stars.

00:18:53.890 --> 00:18:58.030
And Daito wants to help your young, talented troupe grow.

00:18:58.400 --> 00:18:59.460
So, that's all there is to it?

00:18:59.790 --> 00:19:00.860
Don't you like my answer?

00:19:01.260 --> 00:19:06.490
But I swore I'd never act for Daito Entertainment again!

00:19:06.490 --> 00:19:07.850
Take your head out of the clouds.

00:19:07.850 --> 00:19:10.410
Actually, you're not included in this plan.

00:19:11.300 --> 00:19:13.560
Why not?

00:19:13.560 --> 00:19:18.090
What's the problem? Didn't you just say you didn't want to act for Daito again?

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:21.180
But I don't want to be separated from the others!

00:19:21.180 --> 00:19:25.870
We want to further the careers of the others in the troupe. Not yours.

00:19:26.170 --> 00:19:27.820
Are you convinced now?

00:19:30.850 --> 00:19:33.080
It's been a while, Kitajima!

00:19:33.650 --> 00:19:37.020
How are you coming along with that acting award?

00:19:37.520 --> 00:19:41.270
Now you mention it, I hear Ayumi's already been cast as the lead...

00:19:41.270 --> 00:19:44.970
in the Nittei Theater's next spring production.

00:19:44.970 --> 00:19:47.600
And she'll be working with Ms. Tsukikage.

00:19:47.600 --> 00:19:50.600
She is?! Is that true?

00:19:50.600 --> 00:19:55.280
Why don't you go to the Nittei and see for yourself?

00:19:55.280 --> 00:19:59.100
And where are you doing your next show?

00:20:00.220 --> 00:20:01.070
Nowhere.

00:20:01.070 --> 00:20:03.140
Oh, you have no plans!

00:20:03.350 --> 00:20:07.020
I say it's probably high time you finally gave up on <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>!

00:20:07.020 --> 00:20:11.290
How do you plan on winning the Best Actress Award if you can't even get yourself into a show?

00:20:12.300 --> 00:20:17.900
I get it. I'm just in the way for both of you.

00:20:20.280 --> 00:20:25.990
I was an idiot. I had just started to think that you might be decent human beings after all.

00:20:27.210 --> 00:20:31.010
But I'll show both of you.

00:20:31.010 --> 00:20:34.470
I'll show you and I'm keeping my sights firmly on <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>.

00:20:36.410 --> 00:20:39.060
Good. That's the spirit.

00:20:40.430 --> 00:20:42.530
I'd expect nothing less.

00:20:42.530 --> 00:20:46.700
You have a talent for making that girl say the most spectacular things.

00:20:46.700 --> 00:20:48.350
I'm impressed.

00:20:48.960 --> 00:20:50.270
What are you talking about?

00:20:50.270 --> 00:20:55.650
You have a reason for separating her from the rest of her troupe, don't you?

00:20:57.270 --> 00:21:01.860
Anger spurs people to act quicker than sadness.

00:21:01.860 --> 00:21:11.480
You've riled her and directed her towards the Nittei Theater where trouble's brewing.

00:21:14.800 --> 00:21:17.570
You say you put Yukari Kitazono in the pamphlet?

00:21:17.790 --> 00:21:20.270
Well, she's out of the show, so can you take it out?

00:21:20.740 --> 00:21:24.280
Ayumi and Ms. Tsukikage are working together.

00:21:25.250 --> 00:21:30.250
Play: <i>The Two Princesses</i>
The role of Aldis
Open Audition
Please inquire at the front desk for further information.

00:21:30.630 --> 00:21:34.260
An audition to star alongside Ayumi.

00:21:34.690 --> 00:21:41.860
Maya has been cut off from the Athena Theater, but has a new path now opened up for her at last?

00:21:42.520 --> 00:21:49.490
And what is Masumi planning to achieve by cutting Maya from the Athena Theater performance?

00:22:03.940 --> 00:22:18.080
Chikazukitai noni toozaketeshimau

00:22:03.940 --> 00:22:18.080
I want to be close to you, but you're distancing yourself.

00:22:18.080 --> 00:22:31.320
Dakishimetai toki wazato hanareteshimau

00:22:18.080 --> 00:22:31.320
When I want to hold you, you deliberately run away.

00:22:31.320 --> 00:22:44.070
Marude jishaku no N to N no you da ne

00:22:31.320 --> 00:22:44.070
We're like two poles on a magnet...

00:22:44.070 --> 00:22:55.190
Otagai amari nimo nisugita seikana?

00:22:44.070 --> 00:22:55.190
Maybe we're too alike?

00:22:55.190 --> 00:23:09.920
Motto motto sunao na hitomi de mitsureba

00:22:55.190 --> 00:23:09.920
If you allow your eyes to see the truth,

00:23:09.920 --> 00:23:21.510
Yodonderu izumi mo suki tooru hazusa

00:23:09.920 --> 00:23:21.510
even quagmires will become crystal clear.

00:23:24.570 --> 00:23:26.520
Hate me, little one.

00:23:27.550 --> 00:23:31.620
My role right now is to ignite your fighting spirit.

00:23:32.200 --> 00:23:35.730
If you can win the role opposite Ayumi in <i>The Two Princesses</i>,

00:23:35.730 --> 00:23:38.050
then the path to <i>The Scarlet Angel</i> will open up to you again.

00:23:39.230 --> 00:23:40.980
Believe in yourself!

00:23:41.530 --> 00:23:43.230
You have the strength you need!

00:23:44.720 --> 00:23:48.300
I'm always watching over you through Hijiri.

00:23:44.950 --> 00:23:51.500
Episode 34 - Maya's Challenge
